            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BAL03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Ballantyne</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1774-05-13">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1821-06-16"/>
                    <occupation>publisher and literary agent</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ballantyne worked for his brother, <persName key="BAL02">James</persName>, in his Edinburgh publishing house from 1805. He also 
    wrote a novel and contributed ballads to the <title>Edinburgh Annual Register</title>. He first called on Godwin with <persName key="STO01">John Stoddart</persName>,
    recently returned from his tour of Scotland.</p>
                        <p>It is thought that references to 'Ballantine' originally refer to James and then to John. Godwin's initial contact is with 
      James but in 1816 it seems more than probable 
      from the entry for 21 April that the primary relationship by then is with John.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
